From 3a6bdc38a1cd2090d1820a7f4d602206b9079c2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken5998 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:18:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(linux): build natively on arm64 linux handhelds

ArmadaOS and other aarch64 Linux systems on Snapdragon handhelds
had no build path: setup stopped at host_platform. ShiftGlue already
has a linux-arm64 preset, so add the game's linux-arm64 presets, a
toolchain file that uses the pinned LLVM 20.1.8 for ARM64 against the
host's own headers (no Steam Runtime sysroot exists for ARM64), and
setup support that provisions it, links a working ld.lld and names
the Fedora packages to install when development files are missing.

Tests: cross-built ShiftGlue and the host tests for aarch64-linux-gnu
with LLVM 20.1.8; 11 of 11 host tests pass under qemu-aarch64
