@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+# ARM64 Linux handhelds (ArmadaOS)
+
+Pinyon Shift builds natively for ARM64 (aarch64) Linux: the same recompiled
+game as on x86-64 Linux, compiled for the handheld's own CPU and rendered with
+Mesa's Turnip Vulkan driver. Nothing runs through FEX or Box64. This page
+covers [ArmadaOS](https://armadaos.dev/) on Snapdragon handhelds such as the
+Retroid Pocket 6 (Snapdragon 8 Gen 2, Adreno 740); other Fedora-based or
+Debian-based ARM64 distributions work the same way.
+
+> **Status: experimental.** The ShiftGlue translator, runtime, GPU plugin and
+> the host tests cross-compile for aarch64-linux-gnu with the pinned LLVM
+> 20.1.8. A full game build and play session on a device has not been
+> recorded yet; the Android build on the same chips holds about 60 fps with
+> SMOOTH 60.
+
+## What you need
+
+- An ARM64 handheld with a Vulkan 1.3 driver (Mesa Turnip on Adreno 7xx).
+- 8 GB of memory or more; the build uses about 1.5 GB per compile job.
+- About 35 GB free for the first build.
+- Your ISO of the USA retail disc (`MS-2505`).
+
+There is no Steam Runtime sysroot for ARM64, so the build uses the system's
+own headers and libraries. ArmadaOS is image-based and ships without
+compilers, so the build runs inside a **distrobox** of the same Fedora
+release, and the game then runs on the host.
+
+## Build in a distrobox
+
+In Desktop Mode, open Konsole:
+
+```bash
+distrobox create --name pinyon --image registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora-toolbox:44
+distrobox enter pinyon
+```
+
+Inside the box, install the build dependencies (the same list setup prints if
+something is missing):
+
+```bash
+sudo dnf install -y gcc-c++ libstdc++-static glibc-devel lld git python3 \
+  pkgconf-pkg-config libX11-devel libxcb-devel libXext-devel libXcursor-devel \
+  libXi-devel libXrandr-devel libXScrnSaver-devel libXfixes-devel libXtst-devel \
+  libxkbcommon-devel wayland-devel wayland-protocols-devel libdecor-devel \
+  mesa-libEGL-devel mesa-libGL-devel mesa-libgbm-devel libdrm-devel \
+  alsa-lib-devel pulseaudio-libs-devel pipewire-devel systemd-devel dbus-devel
+```
+
+Then clone this repository into your home folder (the box shares it with the
+host) and build:
+
+```bash
+git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/arcanite24/pinyon-shift ~/PinyonShift
+cd ~/PinyonShift
+python3 tools/pinyon.py setup --iso ~/Downloads/forza-horizon.iso
+```
+
+`setup` downloads the pinned CMake, Ninja and LLVM 20.1.8 for ARM64 into
+`.local/toolchain`, links the distribution's `ld.lld` (the LLVM release's
+needs `libxml2.so.2`), reads and checks the disc, translates the game and
+builds `out/build/linux-arm64-release/pinyon_shift`. Keep the device on its
+charger. Pass `--jobs 4` if the box runs out of memory.
+
+## Play
+
+Leave the box (`exit`) and start the game on the host:
+
+```bash
+cd ~/PinyonShift
+python3 tools/pinyon.py launch
+```
+
+`python3 tools/pinyon.py shortcuts add`, also on the host, adds the game to
+the applications menu and to Steam as a non-Steam game for Gaming Mode.
+
+The libstdc++ is linked statically; the game needs only glibc, X11 or
+Wayland client libraries and the Vulkan driver from the host, which ArmadaOS
+has.
+
+## Settings for a Snapdragon 8 Gen 2
+
+The handheld presets of the Android build are not in the desktop settings
+menu. Start from **F6 > GRAPHICS > GRAPHICS PRESET > LOW-SPEC 60** at 1x, and
+set **SCENE SHADING > COARSE**. Android preallocates 256 MB of texture memory
+to avoid stalls on Adreno; the same works here:
+
+```bash
+python3 tools/pinyon.py launch -- --vulkan_texture_memory_prealloc_mb=256
+```
+
+## Not done yet
+
+- A prebuilt ARM64 launcher; the build runs from a terminal.
+- Measurements on a device (frame rate, memory, thermals).
+- Launching from Steam's Gaming Mode on ArmadaOS, where Steam itself runs
+  under FEX, has not been verified.
